      "alt": "A chessboard where each square shows the number of rice grains doubling: 1, 2, 4, 8 and so on. The last square holds about 9.2 quintillion grains.",
      "caption": "Each square holds twice as many grains as the one before."
    },
    {
      "id": "s-first",
      "type": "section",
      "title": "1. A slow start",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "first-row",
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "On square $n$ there are\n\n$$\ng(n) = 2^{\\,n-1}\n$$\n\ngrains. The first row of eight squares holds just $1 + 2 + 4 + \\dots + 128 = 255$ grains, about a teaspoon. Nothing to worry about yet."
        },
