            },
            {
              "x": 12,
              "y": 4095
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "why-sum",
          "type": "reveal",
          "title": "Why is the total one less than the next square?",
          "content": "Call the total $S = 1 + 2 + 4 + \\dots + 2^{n-1}$. Double it:\n\n$$\n2S = 2 + 4 + \\dots + 2^{n}\n$$\n\nSubtract the first line from the second. Almost everything cancels, leaving $2S - S = 2^{n} - 1$, so $S = 2^{n} - 1$."
        },
        {
          "id": "scale",
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "warning",
          "title": "How much rice is that?",
          "content": "At about 25 mg per grain, the board needs roughly **460 billion tonnes** of rice: around 600 years of today's entire world harvest."
        },
        {
          "id": "quiz-total",
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "What is the total number of grains on the first 10 squares?",
          "options": [
            "512",
            "1,000",
            "1,023",
            "1,024"
          ],
          "correctIndex": 2,
          "explanation": "Total = 2¹⁰ − 1 = 1,023, one less than the 1,024 grains that would go on square 11."
        }
      ]
    },
