    {
      "id": "s-real",
      "type": "section",
      "title": "4. Doubling in the real world",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "rule70",
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Anything growing by a fixed **percentage** grows exponentially: bacteria, savings with compound interest, viral videos. A handy estimate is the **rule of 70**:\n\n$$\n\\text{doubling time} \\approx \\frac{70}{\\text{growth rate in \\%}}\n$$\n\nAt 7% interest per year, your money doubles in about 10 years."
        },
        {
          "id": "quiz-70",
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "A city's population grows 2% per year. Roughly how long until it doubles?",
          "options": [
            "2 years",
            "20 years",
            "35 years",
            "70 years"
          ],
          "correctIndex": 2,
          "explanation": "Rule of 70: 70 ÷ 2 = 35 years."
        }
      ]
    },
